        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="GOO01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Alderman</roleName>
                        <forename>Samuel</forename>
                        <surname>Goodbehere</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1818-11-18"/>
                    <occupation>member of the Corporation of London for the Ward of Cheap</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p><title>The Times</title>, reports his death on 20 November 1818, 'Alderman Goodbehere had been
    for nearly thirty years a distinguished member of the Corporation of London', where
    he was an ally of the radical Robert Waithman. The <title>Morning Chronicle</title>, 28 November 1818,
    lists Waithman and Alderman Wood amongst those at his funeral. Godwin records
    his death.  The identification is confirmed by 17 January 1815: 'Court of Aldermen; adv. Goodbehere, Reeves, 
    Thos Bell and Line'. </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="journalism"><title>The Times</title>, 20 November 1818</bibl>
                    <bibl type="journalism"><title>Morning Chronicle</title>, 28 November 1818.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
